Hebrish for Ubuntu
==================

  /usr/bin/hebrish         the app (window + tray)
  /usr/bin/hebrish-model   model CLI: list | use | status | check | download [<model>] [--replace]
  /usr/lib/hebrish/        app code + bundled sherpa-onnx and onnxruntime (not in Ubuntu)
  ~/.config/hebrish/       config.json
  ~/.local/share/hebrish/  models/<model>/<version>/, state.json

Installs alongside the separate "parlance" package (Parlance 0.2.0 upgrades the 0.1.x
parlance builds of this app). On first start Hebrish copies ~/.config/parlance/config.json
(minus the hotkey), history and state, and hardlinks ~/.local/share/parlance/models, so no
model is downloaded twice; Parlance's folders are left as they are. Default hotkey: F14
(Parlance uses F13; both apps would react to a shared key).

Pick a model in the Model tab; each is ~660 MB and downloads once. For the hotkey, join the input
group and log in again:  sudo usermod -aG input $USER
The bundled wheels match the python3 minor version the package was built for;
rebuild after Ubuntu moves python3 to a new minor version.
